cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TimeGym, cite the software and record the version and source commit
  or the source fingerprint in your report. The v2 manuscript is a working paper;
  this metadata does not assert a published v2 release or DOI.
type: software
title: "TimeGym: verification and diagnosis for forecasting pipelines"
authors:
  - family-names: Seca
    given-names: Diogo
repository-code: "https://github.com/diogoseca/timegym"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - time series
  - forecasting
  - verification
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - scientific software
abstract: >-
  TimeGym checks forecasting output contracts, conditional references, and
  declared metamorphic properties. It supports point forecasts, marginal
  quantiles, coherent joint samples, retained visual experiments, and JSON
  diagnostic reports with replay information.
